# Personal identities allowed to SSH into this machine (home role only).
#
# One 1Password item title per line, vault "Personal" assumed. sshconfig.sh
# fetches each item's public key and appends it to ~/.ssh/authorized_keys.
#
# Deliberately a separate list from config/1password/agent.toml.home: that
# file is an *outbound* allowlist (which keys 1Password offers as this
# machine's identity), this one is *inbound* (who's allowed to log in as
# this user). They happen to overlap today, but "unifi ssh key" in the
# outbound list is the router's key, not a client identity -- it has no
# business here.

SSH Key (ed25519)
Personal SSH (rsa)
